  "construction": "Single constraints use event (0,1) and condition (0,2). The two-factor cell adds a second multiply of the same event when (1,2) is present. The two-event cell puts a factor-5 multiply on (1,2) when (0,1) is present. The length-6 list follows complete-edge order (0,1), (0,2), (1,2): for each edge i, a prohibit when edge i+1 (mod 3) is present, then a multiply by 2, 3, or 5 when edge i+2 (mod 3) is present. Length 4 is the prefix. Length 8 appends a factor-4 multiply of (0,1) when (0,2) is absent, then a dissolve prohibit of (0,2) when (1,2) is present. Cardinality 6 counts constraints. It is not a six-node target.",
